  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed extension, due to its excessive width at first floor, proximity to the flank boundary and unsympathetic roof design to the side of the property, would appear as an excessive development that is out of keeping with the roof form of the host dwelling and surrounding area. The proposal would fail to respect the prevailing pattern of development, which is limited to modest ground floor extensions and loft conversions with dormer extensions at the rear and hip to gable roof form, contained within the envelope of the host property. The development would dominate the host building and result in an overdevelopment of this prominent site, creating an incongruous form of development that harms the openness of the site as viewed from the nearby junction and rear streetscene to the southwest of the site, and would be out of keeping with the character of the surrounding area. As such, the proposal is contrary to Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018 and the guidance in Supplementary Planning Documents SPD4 'Design of Residential Extensions' and SPD14 'Creating Locally Distinctive Places'."
  ],
